PMB OS: a software MIDI synthesizer in winealsa.drv for systems without an ALSA sequencer.

Android has no ALSA sequencer, so Wine offered no MIDI out device at all: MIDI music (RPG Maker 2000/2003/XP,
many older games) stayed silent or the program failed. When PMBOS_SOUNDFONT names a SoundFont 2 file, a device
"PMB OS Synth" is offered instead; while open it renders with TinySoundFont (tsf.h, MIT, copied into
dlls/winealsa.drv by the pack builder) to the ALSA PCM "default" (PMB OS: the app's sound server). GM / GS / XG
reset SysEx restore the defaults; channel 10 plays drums.

